{"toolCallId":"call_4bfc97e25b3748a8bcf9fc5f1363d533","title":"Wrote ./specs/zz-bench-authoring/001-recommend-level-quiet-flag/plan.md","kind":"edit","content":[{"type":"diff","path":"/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-michelkerkmeester-MEGA-Development-Code-Environment-Public/fcd93cd7-b3f2-45e6-b976-87fabe792df3/scratchpad/speed-loop/w1eb206b128/tree/specs/zz-bench-authoring/001-recommend-level-quiet-flag/plan.md","oldText":"---\ntitle: \"Implementation Plan: Add a quiet flag to recommend-level.sh\"\ndescription: \"[2-3 sentences: what this implements and the technical approach]\"\ntrigger_phrases:\n  - \"recommend level quiet flag plan\"\nimportance_tier: \"normal\"\ncontextType: \"general\"\n---\n<!-- SPECKIT_TEMPLATE_SOURCE: plan-core | v2.3 -->\n# Implementation Plan: Add a quiet flag to recommend-level.sh\n\n<!-- SPECKIT_LEVEL: 3 -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:summary -->\n## 1. SUMMARY\n<!-- FILL: Fill the stack row and write three sentences: what changes, where, and how you will prove it. GOOD: Change one bash script. Add one output branch. Prove it with a line count. WEAK: This plan describes the implementation. -->\n\n### Technical Context\n\n| Aspect | Value |\n|--------|-------|\n| **Language/Stack** | [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: e.g., TypeScript, Python 3.11] |\n| **Framework** | [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: e.g., React, FastAPI] |\n| **Storage** | [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: e.g., PostgreSQL, None] |\n| **Testing** | [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: e.g., Jest, pytest] |\n\n### Overview\n[2-3 sentences: what this implements and the technical approach]\n<!-- /ANCHOR:summary -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:quality-gates -->\n## 2. QUALITY GATES\n<!-- FILL: Turn each gate into a check a command can answer. Keep the boxes unticked until they pass. GOOD: `rg -n 'quiet' recommend-level.sh` prints the new branch before the task starts. WEAK: The team agrees the plan is ready. -->\n\n### Definition of Ready\n- [ ] Problem statement clear and scope documented\n- [ ] Success criteria measurable\n- [ ] Dependencies identified\n\n### Definition of Done\n- [ ] All acceptance criteria met\n- [ ] Tests passing (if applicable)\n- [ ] Docs updated (spec/plan/tasks)\n<!-- /ANCHOR:quality-gates -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:architecture -->\n## 3. ARCHITECTURE\n<!-- FILL: Name the pattern in three words, then list the one component that changes. GOOD: Single script branch. The component is `recommend-level.sh`. WEAK: Standard architecture. -->\n\n### Pattern\n[YOUR_VALUE_HERE: MVC | MVVM | Clean Architecture | Serverless | Monolith | Other]\n\n### Key Components\n- **[YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Component 1]**: [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Purpose]\n- **[YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Component 2]**: [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Purpose]\n\n### Data Flow\n[YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Brief description of how data moves through the system]\n<!-- /ANCHOR:architecture -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:affected-surfaces -->\n## FIX ADDENDUM: AFFECTED SURFACES\n<!-- FILL: Name each surface the change touches. Write `not a consumer` when it does not read the change. Write `N/A` or delete the whole addendum when no fix surface applies. GOOD: `recommend-level.sh`: owns the output. Action: update. WEAK: Various files. -->\n\nUse this section when `research_intent=fix_bug`, when planning from a deep-review FAIL/CONDITIONAL verdict, or when any finding touches security, path handling, env precedence, schema boundaries, persistence, public responses, or shared policy.\n\n| Surface | Current Role | Action | Verification |\n|---------|--------------|--------|--------------|\n| [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: producer/helper/policy] | [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: what owns the behavior] | [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: update/unchanged/not a consumer] | [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: grep/test/doc evidence] |\n| [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: consumer/status/docs/tests] | [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: how it observes the behavior] | [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: update/unchanged/not a consumer] | [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: grep/test/doc evidence] |\n\nRequired inventories:\n- Same-class producers: `rg -n '<field|string|helper|literal|error-pattern>' <module-or-files>`.\n- Consumers of changed symbols: `rg -n '<changedSymbol>|<changedConstant>|<changedPublicField>' . --glob '*.ts' --glob '*.js' --glob '*.md'`.\n- Matrix axes: list every independent input axis and the required rows before implementation.\n- Algorithm invariant: for path/redaction/parser/resolver/security fixes, state the invariant and adversarial cases.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:affected-surfaces -->\n\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:phases -->\n## 4. IMPLEMENTATION PHASES\n<!-- FILL: Point to `tasks.md` and name the three phases in one line. GOOD: Setup reads the current output. Implementation adds the branch. Verification counts lines. WEAK: See tasks. -->\n\nFollow the ordered tasks in `tasks.md`. It owns the Setup, Implementation and Verification phase checkboxes and task state.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:phases -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:testing -->\n## 5. TESTING STRATEGY\n<!-- FILL: Name the one command you will run and the output it must print. GOOD: `--quiet` prints 1 line. The default prints 17. WEAK: Test it manually. -->\n\n| Test Type | Scope | Tools |\n|-----------|-------|-------|\n| Unit | [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Components/functions] | [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Jest/pytest/etc.] |\n| Integration | [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: API endpoints/flows] | [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Tools] |\n| Manual | [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: User journeys] | Browser |\n<!-- /ANCHOR:testing -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:dependencies -->\n## 6. DEPENDENCIES\n<!-- FILL: List each tool the change needs, or write `None`. GOOD: `bash` and `awk`. No new package. WEAK: Usual dependencies. -->\n\n| Dependency | Type | Status | Impact if Blocked |\n|------------|------|--------|-------------------|\n| [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: System/Library] | [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Internal/External] | [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Green/Yellow/Red] | [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Impact] |\n<!-- /ANCHOR:dependencies -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:rollback -->\n## 7. ROLLBACK PLAN\n<!-- FILL: Name the trigger and the one command that reverts the change. GOOD: Trigger: the default output changes. Revert the one commit. WEAK: Roll back if needed. -->\n\n- **Trigger**: [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Conditions requiring rollback]\n- **Procedure**: [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: How to revert changes]\n<!-- /ANCHOR:rollback -->\n\n---\n\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:phase-deps -->\n## L2: PHASE DEPENDENCIES\n<!-- FILL: Draw the phase order in the fence, then fill the table with depends-on and blocks. Write `N/A` with one reason, or delete the whole section. GOOD: Setup to Implementation to Verification. Verification blocks close. WEAK: Phases depend on each other. -->\n\n```\nPhase 1 (Setup) ──────┐\n                      ├──► Phase 2 (Core) ──► Phase 3 (Verify)\nPhase 1.5 (Config) ───┘\n```\n\n| Phase | Depends On | Blocks |\n|-------|------------|--------|\n| Setup | None | Core, Config |\n| Config | Setup | Core |\n| Core | Setup, Config | Verify |\n| Verify | Core | None |\n<!-- /ANCHOR:phase-deps -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:effort -->\n## L2: EFFORT ESTIMATION\n<!-- FILL: Give each phase an estimate and a total. Mark the total as an assumption. Write `N/A` with one reason, or delete the whole section. GOOD: Setup 10 minutes, implementation 30, verification 10. Total 50 minutes. WEAK: A few hours. -->\n\n| Phase | Complexity | Estimated Effort |\n|-------|------------|------------------|\n| Setup | [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Low/Med/High] | [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: e.g., 1-2 hours] |\n| Core Implementation | [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Low/Med/High] | [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: e.g., 4-8 hours] |\n| Verification | [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Low/Med/High] | [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: e.g., 1-2 hours] |\n| **Total** | | **[YOUR_VALUE_HERE: e.g., 6-12 hours]** |\n<!-- /ANCHOR:effort -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:enhanced-rollback -->\n## L2: ENHANCED ROLLBACK\n<!-- FILL: Name the trigger, the steps and the data reversal. Write `No` when no data changes. Delete the whole section when the packet ships no deployable service. GOOD: Trigger: default output changes. Steps: revert one commit, rerun the two commands. WEAK: Roll back if needed. -->\n\n### Pre-deployment Checklist\n- [ ] Backup created (if data changes)\n- [ ] Feature flag configured\n- [ ] Monitoring alerts set\n\n### Rollback Procedure\n1. [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Immediate action - e.g., disable feature flag]\n2. [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Revert code - e.g., git revert or redeploy previous version]\n3. [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Verify rollback - e.g., smoke test critical paths]\n4. [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Notify stakeholders - if user-facing]\n\n### Data Reversal\n- **Has data migrations?** [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Yes/No]\n- **Reversal procedure**: [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Steps or \"N/A\"]\n<!-- /ANCHOR:enhanced-rollback -->\n\n---\n\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:dependency-graph -->\n## L3: DEPENDENCY GRAPH\n<!-- FILL: Draw the component order and fill the matrix with produces and blocks. Write `N/A` with one reason, or delete the whole section. GOOD: Script to test to close. WEAK: Components depend on each other. -->\n\n```\n┌─────────────┐     ┌─────────────┐     ┌─────────────┐\n│   Phase 1   │────►│   Phase 2   │────►│   Phase 3   │\n│   Setup     │     │    Core     │     │   Verify    │\n└─────────────┘     └──────┬──────┘     └─────────────┘\n                          │\n                    ┌─────▼─────┐\n                    │  Phase 2b │\n                    │  Parallel │\n                    └───────────┘\n```\n\n### Dependency Matrix\n\n| Component | Depends On | Produces | Blocks |\n|-----------|------------|----------|--------|\n| [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Component A] | None | [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Output] | B, C |\n| [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Component B] | A | [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Output] | D |\n| [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Component C] | A | [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Output] | D |\n| [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Component D] | B, C | [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Final] | None |\n<!-- /ANCHOR:dependency-graph -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:critical-path -->\n## L3: CRITICAL PATH\n<!-- FILL: Name the longest chain and its total. List what can run in parallel. Write `N/A` with one reason, or delete the whole section. GOOD: Implementation to verification, 40 minutes. Docs run in parallel. WEAK: The critical path is the main path. -->\n\n1. **[YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Phase/Task]** - [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Duration estimate] - CRITICAL\n2. **[YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Phase/Task]** - [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Duration estimate] - CRITICAL\n3. **[YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Phase/Task]** - [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Duration estimate] - CRITICAL\n\n**Total Critical Path**: [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Sum of durations]\n\n**Parallel Opportunities**:\n- [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Task A] and [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Task B] can run simultaneously\n- [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Task C] and [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Task D] can run after Phase 1\n<!-- /ANCHOR:critical-path -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:milestones -->\n## L3: MILESTONES\n<!-- FILL: Name three milestones with a command-checkable success criterion. Write `N/A` with one reason, or delete the whole section. GOOD: M1: the branch exists. `rg -n quiet` prints it. WEAK: Milestones are tracked. -->\n\n| Milestone | Description | Success Criteria | Target |\n|-----------|-------------|------------------|--------|\n| M1 | [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Setup Complete] | [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: All dependencies ready] | [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Date/Phase] |\n| M2 | [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Core Done] | [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Main features working] | [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Date/Phase] |\n| M3 | [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Release Ready] | [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: All tests pass] | [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Date/Phase] |\n<!-- /ANCHOR:milestones -->\n\n---\n\n## L3: ARCHITECTURE DECISION RECORD\n<!-- FILL: Write one ADR per decision. Name the context, the choice, the consequence and the rejected option. GOOD: ADR-001: a flag, because callers already pass flags. WEAK: We made a decision. -->\n\n### ADR-001: [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Decision Title]\n\n**Status**: [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Proposed/Accepted/Deprecated]\n\n**Context**: [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: What problem we're solving]\n\n**Decision**: [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: What we decided]\n\n**Consequences**:\n- [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Positive outcome 1]\n- [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Negative outcome + mitigation]\n\n**Alternatives Rejected**:\n- [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Option B]: [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Why rejected]\n\n---\n\n","newText":"---\ntitle: \"Implementation Plan: Add a quiet flag to recommend-level.sh\"\ndescription: \"Add one flag to the existing bash parser, one global and one output-dispatch branch in recommend-level.sh. The default report and the JSON payload stay untouched, and a line count plus a baseline diff prove both halves.\"\ntrigger_phrases:\n  - \"recommend level quiet flag plan\"\nimportance_tier: \"normal\"\ncontextType: \"general\"\n---\n<!-- SPECKIT_TEMPLATE_SOURCE: plan-core | v2.3 -->\n# Implementation Plan: Add a quiet flag to recommend-level.sh\n\n<!-- SPECKIT_LEVEL: 3 -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:summary -->\n## 1. SUMMARY\n\n### Technical Context\n\n| Aspect | Value |\n|--------|-------|\n| **Language/Stack** | Bash 3.2+ (macOS `/bin/bash`), coreutils |\n| **Framework** | None - single procedural shell script |\n| **Storage** | None |\n| **Testing** | Direct invocation with `bash -n`, `wc -l`, `diff` and `grep` |\n\n### Overview\n\nChange one file: add a `QUIET_OUTPUT` global, a `--quiet` case in the argument parser, and an output-dispatch branch that prints `Recommended Level: <N> (<Name>)`. `output_text()` and `output_json()` stay untouched, so the default report and the JSON payload cannot drift; verification compares line counts and a baseline diff.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:summary -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:quality-gates -->\n## 2. QUALITY GATES\n\n### Definition of Ready\n- [x] Problem statement clear and scope documented\n- [x] Success criteria measurable\n- [x] Dependencies identified\n\n### Definition of Done\n- [ ] All acceptance criteria met\n- [ ] Tests passing (if applicable)\n- [ ] Docs updated (spec/plan/tasks)\n<!-- /ANCHOR:quality-gates -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:architecture -->\n## 3. ARCHITECTURE\n\n### Pattern\nSingle-script CLI branch (procedural bash).\n\n### Key Components\n- **Argument parser** (`while [[ $# -gt 0 ]]` + `case`): recognizes `--quiet` and sets `QUIET_OUTPUT`.\n- **Globals block**: holds `QUIET_OUTPUT=false` beside `JSON_OUTPUT=false`.\n- **Output dispatch**: chooses `output_json`, the quiet one-liner, or `output_text`.\n- **`output_text()`**: owns the full report and is not modified.\n\n### Data Flow\n\nArguments enter the parser, which sets `LOC`, `FILES`, the risk flags, `JSON_OUTPUT` and `QUIET_OUTPUT`. The scoring helpers and `determine_level` / `determine_phasing` compute the same values in every mode. The dispatch then renders JSON, the single quiet line, or the full report, and the script exits 0.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:architecture -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:affected-surfaces -->\n## FIX ADDENDUM: AFFECTED SURFACES\n\n| Surface | Current Role | Action | Verification |\n|---------|--------------|--------|--------------|\n| `runtime/cli/spec/recommend-level.sh` | Producer: owns the report, JSON payload and exit codes | update | `bash -n` exits 0; `--quiet` prints 1 line; default output diffs clean against the baseline. |\n| `show_help` heredoc and header OPTIONS block | Describe the flag surface | update | `--help \\| grep -- '--quiet'` prints one row; header and heredoc agree. |\n| `runtime/cli/tests/test-phase-system.js` | Consumer: invokes the script with `--json` and parses the payload | not a consumer | Tests pass unchanged; no assertion reads text output. |\n| `README.md` and `references/workflows/*.md` | Describe invocation, never parse output | not a consumer | Invocation examples stay valid; no edit needed. |\n\nRequired inventories:\n- Same-class producers: `rg -n 'JSON_OUTPUT|RECOMMEND_PHASES' runtime/cli/spec/recommend-level.sh` lists the existing output-mode flags.\n- Consumers of changed symbols: `rg -n 'QUIET_OUTPUT|--quiet' .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit` after the change finds only the script and this packet.\n- Matrix axes: output mode (text / JSON) x quiet (on / off) x phase section (on / off), plus flag order for `--quiet --json`.\n- Algorithm invariant: quiet never changes a computed value; it only selects the renderer. Adversarial cases are repeated flags, both flag orders, and `--quiet --help`.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:affected-surfaces -->\n\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:phases -->\n## 4. IMPLEMENTATION PHASES\n\nFollow the ordered tasks in `tasks.md`. It owns the Setup, Implementation and Verification phase checkboxes and task state.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:phases -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:testing -->\n## 5. TESTING STRATEGY\n\n| Test Type | Scope | Tools |\n|-----------|-------|-------|\n| Unit | Parser case and dispatch branch, exercised through the script | `bash -n`, direct invocation |\n| Integration | Full output matrix: text/JSON x quiet on/off x phase on/off | `wc -l`, `diff`, `grep` |\n| Manual | `--help` review and a piped `awk` read of the quiet line | Terminal |\n\nThe load-bearing checks are `--quiet ... | wc -l` printing `1` and a `diff` of the default invocation against a pre-change capture printing nothing.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:testing -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:dependencies -->\n## 6. DEPENDENCIES\n\n| Dependency | Type | Status | Impact if Blocked |\n|------------|------|--------|-------------------|\n| `bash` 3.2+ | Internal | Green | The script already requires it; no new runtime. |\n| coreutils (`wc`, `diff`, `grep`) | Internal | Green | Used for verification only, not by the feature. |\n<!-- /ANCHOR:dependencies -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:rollback -->\n## 7. ROLLBACK PLAN\n\n- **Trigger**: the default report or the JSON payload changes, or `--quiet` prints more than one line.\n- **Procedure**: `git revert` the single commit; the change is additive and touches one file, so there is no data or configuration to unwind.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:rollback -->\n\n---\n\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:phase-deps -->\n## L2: PHASE DEPENDENCIES\n\n```\nPhase 1 (Setup) ──────┐\n                      ├──► Phase 2 (Implementation) ──► Phase 3 (Verification)\nPhase 1.5 (Baseline) ─┘\n```\n\n| Phase | Depends On | Blocks |\n|-------|------------|--------|\n| Setup | None | Baseline, Implementation |\n| Baseline | Setup | Implementation |\n| Implementation | Setup, Baseline | Verification |\n| Verification | Implementation | None |\n<!-- /ANCHOR:phase-deps -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:effort -->\n## L2: EFFORT ESTIMATION\n\n| Phase | Complexity | Estimated Effort |\n|-------|------------|------------------|\n| Setup | Low | 5 minutes |\n| Core Implementation | Low | 15 minutes |\n| Verification | Low | 10 minutes |\n| **Total** | | **~30 minutes (assumption)** |\n<!-- /ANCHOR:effort -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:enhanced-rollback -->\n## L2: ENHANCED ROLLBACK\n\n### Pre-deployment Checklist\n- [ ] Backup created (if data changes) - N/A, no data\n- [ ] Feature flag configured - N/A, the flag is the feature\n- [ ] Monitoring alerts set - N/A, local CLI script\n\n### Rollback Procedure\n1. Revert the single commit with `git revert`.\n2. Re-run `--quiet` and the default form, then compare against the saved baseline.\n3. No stakeholder notification is needed; the script ships in-repo.\n\n### Data Reversal\n- **Has data migrations?** No\n- **Reversal procedure**: N/A\n<!-- /ANCHOR:enhanced-rollback -->\n\n---\n\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:dependency-graph -->\n## L3: DEPENDENCY GRAPH\n\n```\n┌─────────────┐     ┌─────────────┐     ┌─────────────┐\n│   Phase 1   │────►│   Phase 2   │────►│   Phase 3   │\n│   Setup     │     │    Core     │     │   Verify    │\n└─────────────┘     └──────┬──────┘     └─────────────┘\n                          │\n                    ┌─────▼─────┐\n                    │  Baseline │\n                    │  Capture  │\n                    └───────────┘\n```\n\n### Dependency Matrix\n\n| Component | Depends On | Produces | Blocks |\n|-----------|------------|----------|--------|\n| Baseline capture | None | Saved default output for the fixture arguments | Implementation comparison |\n| Parser case | Baseline capture | `QUIET_OUTPUT` set from `--quiet` | Dispatch branch |\n| Dispatch branch | Parser case | One-line quiet output | Verification |\n| Verification | Dispatch branch | Line-count and diff evidence | Packet close |\n<!-- /ANCHOR:dependency-graph -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:critical-path -->\n## L3: CRITICAL PATH\n\n1. **Baseline capture** - 5 minutes - CRITICAL\n2. **Parser case and dispatch branch** - 15 minutes - CRITICAL\n3. **Line-count and diff verification** - 10 minutes - CRITICAL\n\n**Total Critical Path**: ~30 minutes\n\n**Parallel Opportunities**:\n- Help-text edits and the dispatch branch can be written in one pass, then verified together.\n- Packet documentation updates run in parallel with implementation.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:critical-path -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:milestones -->\n## L3: MILESTONES\n\n| Milestone | Description | Success Criteria | Target |\n|-----------|-------------|------------------|--------|\n| M1 | Baseline captured | Default output for `--loc 500 --files 15` saved under `scratch/` | Phase 1 |\n| M2 | Flag implemented | `--quiet` prints exactly one line and exits 0 | Phase 2 |\n| M3 | Verified | AC rows carry evidence and `validate.sh --strict` passes | Phase 3 |\n<!-- /ANCHOR:milestones -->\n\n---\n\n## L3: ARCHITECTURE DECISION RECORD\n\n### ADR-001: Quiet is a dispatch branch, not a guard inside `output_text()`\n\n**Status**: Accepted\n\n**Context**: The flag must produce one line without risking the 16-line default report that callers and docs already rely on.\n\n**Decision**: Add `elif [[ \"$QUIET_OUTPUT\" = true ]]` to the output dispatch and leave `output_text()` untouched.\n\n**Consequences**:\n- The default path is structurally unchanged, so a diff can prove it.\n- The label format is duplicated in one more place; AC-002 pins it, and a shared `printf` becomes worthwhile if a third renderer appears.\n\n**Alternatives Rejected**:\n- Guard at the top of `output_text()`: touches the default function and splits its contract between two branches.\n- `--json | jq`: adds a `jq` dependency for callers and a second process.\n- Environment variable: callers already pass flags, and env state is implicit and harder to test.\n\n---\n\n### ADR-002: `--json` wins over `--quiet`\n\n**Status**: Accepted\n\n**Context**: Both flags select an output format, and a caller can pass both.\n\n**Decision**: Evaluate `JSON_OUTPUT` first; quiet applies to the text report only.\n\n**Consequences**:\n- Passing both stays harmless and JSON parsing keeps working.\n- Quiet is not a universal one-line mode; help and spec say so.\n\n**Alternatives Rejected**:\n- Error on conflict: rejects a harmless combination and adds an exit path.\n- Fold JSON into one line: changes the payload shape and breaks existing parsers.\n\n---\n","_meta":{"cognition.ai/linesAdded":93,"cognition.ai/linesRemoved":83}}],"rawInput":{"file_path":"/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-michelkerkmeester-MEGA-Development-Code-Environment-Public/fcd93cd7-b3f2-45e6-b976-87fabe792df3/scratchpad/speed-loop/w1eb206b128/tree/specs/zz-bench-authoring/001-recommend-level-quiet-flag/plan.md"},"_meta":{"cognition.ai/inferenceToolName":"write"}}
