{"toolCallId":"call_673ddd9114354c1897a0120489349a73","title":"Ran node","kind":"execute","content":[{"type":"content","content":{"type":"resource","resource":{"mimeType":"text/x-shellscript","text":"node --import ./.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/node_modules/tsx/dist/loader.mjs .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/graph/backfill-graph-metadata.ts specs/zz-bench-authoring/001-recommend-level-quiet-flag --dry-run 2>&1","uri":"tool://preview"},"_meta":{"cognition.ai/preview_is_shell_command":true}}}],"rawInput":{"command":"node --import ./.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/node_modules/tsx/dist/loader.mjs .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/graph/backfill-graph-metadata.ts specs/zz-bench-authoring/001-recommend-level-quiet-flag --dry-run 2>&1 | tail -30","workdir":"/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-michelkerkmeester-MEGA-Development-Code-Environment-Public/fcd93cd7-b3f2-45e6-b976-87fabe792df3/scratchpad/speed-loop/w1eb206b128/tree"},"_meta":{"cognition.ai/commandNames":["node"],"cognition.ai/inferenceToolName":"exec"}}
{"toolCallId":"call_74d1116ba6a949fdbb107aafa6930c59","title":"Wrote ./specs/zz-bench-authoring/001-recommend-level-quiet-flag/spec.md","kind":"edit","content":[{"type":"diff","path":"/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-michelkerkmeester-MEGA-Development-Code-Environment-Public/fcd93cd7-b3f2-45e6-b976-87fabe792df3/scratchpad/speed-loop/w1eb206b128/tree/specs/zz-bench-authoring/001-recommend-level-quiet-flag/spec.md","oldText":"---\ntitle: \"Feature Specification: Add a quiet flag to recommend-level.sh\"\ndescription: \"[YOUR_VALUE_HERE: What is broken, missing, or inefficient? 2-3 sentences describing the specific pain point.]\"\ntrigger_phrases:\n  - \"recommend level quiet flag\"\n  - \"add a quiet flag to recommend level sh\"\nimportance_tier: \"normal\"\ncontextType: \"general\"\n---\n<!-- SPECKIT_TEMPLATE_SOURCE: spec-core + level2-verify + level3-arch | v2.3 -->\n# Feature Specification: Add a quiet flag to recommend-level.sh\n\n<!-- SPECKIT_LEVEL: 3 -->\n\n\n---\n\n## EXECUTIVE SUMMARY\n<!-- FILL: Write three sentences: the problem, the change and the proof. GOOD: Callers parse a 17-line report to read one value. The flag prints one line. A line count proves it. WEAK: This document describes the feature. -->\n\n[2-3 sentence high-level overview for stakeholders who need quick context]\n\n**Key Decisions**: [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Major decision 1], [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Major decision 2]\n\n**Critical Dependencies**: [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Blocking dependency]\n\n---\n<!-- ANCHOR:metadata -->\n## 1. METADATA\n<!-- FILL: Fill every row: level, priority, status, date and branch. Use the real branch name. GOOD: Priority P1. Status Draft. Branch `feat/recommend-level-quiet`. WEAK: Priority TBD. Status maybe. -->\n\n| Field | Value |\n|-------|-------|\n| **Level** | 3 |\n| **Priority** | [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: P0/P1/P2] |\n| **Status** | Draft |\n| **Created** | 2026-10-26 |\n| **Branch** | `scaffold/001-recommend-level-quiet-flag` |\n<!-- /ANCHOR:metadata -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:problem -->\n## 2. PROBLEM & PURPOSE\n<!-- FILL: State the problem in two sentences: what breaks, and for whom. GOOD: The recommend-level script prints a 17-line report, so a caller that needs only the level cannot parse the answer. WEAK: The script has issues with output. -->\n\n### Problem Statement\n[YOUR_VALUE_HERE: What is broken, missing, or inefficient? 2-3 sentences describing the specific pain point.]\n\n### Purpose\n[YOUR_VALUE_HERE: One-sentence outcome statement. What does success look like?]\n<!-- /ANCHOR:problem -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:scope -->\n## 3. SCOPE\n<!-- FILL: List three to five things this change does, each starting with a verb. GOOD: Add a `--quiet` flag that prints only the recommended-level line. WEAK: Update the script and docs. -->\n\n### In Scope\n- [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Deliverable 1]\n- [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Deliverable 2]\n- [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Deliverable 3]\n\n### Out of Scope\n- [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Excluded item 1] - [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: why]\n- [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Excluded item 2] - [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: why]\n\n### Files to Change\n\n| File Path | Change Type | Description |\n|-----------|-------------|-------------|\n| [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: path/to/file.js] | [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Modify/Create/Delete] | [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Brief description] |\n<!-- /ANCHOR:scope -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:requirements -->\n## 4. REQUIREMENTS\n<!-- FILL: Write one testable requirement per row. Name the exact command or output. GOOD: With `--quiet`, stdout holds exactly one line that starts with `Recommended Level:`. WEAK: The flag should work well. -->\n\n### P0 - Blockers (MUST complete)\n\n| ID | Requirement |\n|----|-------------|\n| REQ-001 | [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Requirement description] |\n\n### P1 - Required (complete OR user-approved deferral)\n\n| ID | Requirement |\n|----|-------------|\n| REQ-002 | [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Requirement description] |\n\n> Acceptance criteria for these requirements live in `acceptance-criteria.md`,\n> which is the document that decides whether this packet may close.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:requirements -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:success-criteria -->\n## 5. SUCCESS CRITERIA\n<!-- FILL: Write one measurable outcome per line. A command can prove it. GOOD: `recommend-level.sh --quiet --loc 500 --files 15` prints one line and exits 0. WEAK: The feature is successful. -->\n\n- **SC-001**: [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Primary measurable outcome]\n- **SC-002**: [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Secondary measurable outcome]\n<!-- /ANCHOR:success-criteria -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:risks -->\n## 6. RISKS & DEPENDENCIES\n<!-- FILL: Name one dependency and one risk. Give each a concrete mitigation. GOOD: A caller parses the level line and breaks when the label changes. Mitigation: keep the label stable and test it. WEAK: There may be some risk. -->\n\n| Type | Item | Impact | Mitigation |\n|------|------|--------|------------|\n| Dependency | [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: System/API] | [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: What if blocked] | [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Fallback plan] |\n| Risk | [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Risk description] | [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: High/Med/Low] | [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Mitigation strategy] |\n<!-- /ANCHOR:risks -->\n\n---\n\n\n## 7. NON-FUNCTIONAL REQUIREMENTS\n<!-- FILL: Name one measurable limit per line. Write `N/A` and one reason when the packet runs no service, or delete the whole section. GOOD: The flag adds no measurable time: the same 40 ms run. WEAK: Performance is good. -->\n\n### Performance\n- **NFR-P01**: [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Response time target - e.g., <200ms p95]\n\n### Security\n- **NFR-S01**: [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Auth requirement - e.g., JWT tokens required]\n\n### Reliability\n- **NFR-R01**: [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Uptime target - e.g., 99.9%]\n\n---\n\n## 8. EDGE CASES\n<!-- FILL: Name the empty input, the maximum input and the failure path. One line each. GOOD: Empty input: the script exits 2 with usage. Maximum: 10,000 files scores in under one second. WEAK: Handle edge cases. -->\n\n### Data Boundaries\n- Empty input: [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: How system handles]\n- Maximum length: [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Limit and behavior]\n\n### Error Scenarios\n- External service failure: [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Fallback behavior]\n- Network timeout: [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Retry strategy]\n\n### State Transitions\n- Partial completion: [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Recovery behavior]\n- Session expiry: [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: User experience]\n\n---\n\n## 9. COMPLEXITY ASSESSMENT\n<!-- FILL: Score each row with the number the change earns. The total must match the level. GOOD: Scope 4/25: one file and 12 lines. Total 18/100. WEAK: Complexity is medium. -->\n\n| Dimension | Score | Triggers |\n|-----------|-------|----------|\n| Scope | [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: /25] | [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Files: X, LOC: Y, Systems: Z] |\n| Risk | [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: /25] | [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Auth: Y/N, API: Y/N, Breaking: Y/N] |\n| Research | [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: /20] | [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Investigation needs] |\n| Multi-Agent | [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: /15] | [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Workstreams: X] |\n| Coordination | [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: /15] | [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Dependencies: X] |\n| **Total** | **[YOUR_VALUE_HERE: /100]** | **Level 3** |\n\n---\n\n## 10. RISK MATRIX\n<!-- FILL: List each risk with impact, likelihood and one mitigation. GOOD: R1: a caller parses the label. Impact M, likelihood L. Mitigation: a test pins the label. WEAK: Some risks exist. -->\n\n| Risk ID | Description | Impact | Likelihood | Mitigation |\n|---------|-------------|--------|------------|------------|\n| R-001 | [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Risk] | [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: H/M/L] | [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: H/M/L] | [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Strategy] |\n\n---\n\n## 11. USER STORIES\n<!-- FILL: Write one story per user. Name the actor, the want and the benefit. GOOD: As a build script, I want one parseable line, so that I can skip the report. WEAK: Users want a quiet mode. -->\n\n### US-001: [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Title] (Priority: P0)\n\n**As a** [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: user type], **I want** [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: needed behavior], **so that** [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: benefit].\n\n**Acceptance criteria:** see `acceptance-criteria.md` (rows referencing this story).\n\n---\n\n### US-002: [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Title] (Priority: P1)\n\n**As a** [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: user type], **I want** [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: needed behavior], **so that** [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: benefit].\n\n**Acceptance criteria:** see `acceptance-criteria.md` (rows referencing this story).\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:questions -->\n## 12. OPEN QUESTIONS\n<!-- FILL: Write each open question as one line. Write `None` when nothing blocks. GOOD: Does `--quiet` suppress warnings? No, stderr is unchanged. WEAK: Edge cases are unclear. -->\n\n- [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Question 1 requiring clarification]\n- [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Question 2 requiring clarification]\n<!-- /ANCHOR:questions -->\n\n---\n\n## RELATED DOCUMENTS\n<!-- FILL: Leave the four links in place. -->\n\n- **Implementation Plan**: See `plan.md`\n- **Task Breakdown**: See `tasks.md`\n- **Verification Checklist**: See `tasks.md`\n- **Decision Records**: See `decision-record.md`\n\n---\n\n\n","newText":"---\ntitle: \"Feature Specification: Add a quiet flag to recommend-level.sh\"\ndescription: \"recommend-level.sh prints a 16-line report for every text invocation, so a caller that needs only the level must parse the report or take the JSON payload. A --quiet flag prints just the recommended-level line and leaves the default report unchanged.\"\ntrigger_phrases:\n  - \"recommend level quiet flag\"\n  - \"add a quiet flag to recommend level sh\"\nimportance_tier: \"normal\"\ncontextType: \"general\"\n---\n<!-- SPECKIT_TEMPLATE_SOURCE: spec-core + level2-verify + level3-arch | v2.3 -->\n# Feature Specification: Add a quiet flag to recommend-level.sh\n\n<!-- SPECKIT_LEVEL: 3 -->\n\n\n---\n\n## EXECUTIVE SUMMARY\n\nCallers that need the recommended level today either parse a 16-line report or switch to JSON and extract one field. `--quiet` prints the single `Recommended Level: N (Name)` line and leaves every other output path byte-identical. A line count and a baseline diff prove both halves.\n\n**Key Decisions**: `--quiet` selects a text-output branch, so `--json` wins when both are passed; the quiet line is rendered in the output dispatch, leaving `output_text()` untouched.\n\n**Critical Dependencies**: None beyond the bash 3.2+ and coreutils the script already uses.\n\n---\n<!-- ANCHOR:metadata -->\n## 1. METADATA\n\n| Field | Value |\n|-------|-------|\n| **Level** | 3 |\n| **Priority** | P2 |\n| **Status** | Draft |\n| **Created** | 2026-10-26 |\n| **Branch** | `scaffold/001-recommend-level-quiet-flag` |\n<!-- /ANCHOR:metadata -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:problem -->\n## 2. PROBLEM & PURPOSE\n\n### Problem Statement\n\n`recommend-level.sh` prints a 16-line report for a text invocation, or 12 lines with `--no-recommend-phases`. A caller that needs only the level, such as a CI step or a wrapper choosing a documentation depth, must parse the report or take the 36-line JSON payload and extract `recommended_level` from it.\n\n### Purpose\n\nAdd one flag that prints the recommended-level line and nothing else, so a caller can read the level with `awk`, `sed`, or command substitution without parsing the report.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:problem -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:scope -->\n## 3. SCOPE\n\n### In Scope\n- Recognize `--quiet` in the existing argument parser and track it in a `QUIET_OUTPUT` global that defaults to false.\n- Print exactly `Recommended Level: <N> (<Name>)` and exit 0 when `--quiet` is set and JSON output is not requested.\n- Document the flag in the header OPTIONS block and in the `show_help` heredoc.\n- Keep the default report, the JSON payload, scoring, phase logic, stderr messages and exit codes unchanged.\n\n### Out of Scope\n- A short alias such as `-q` - not requested, and the parser already spends `-j` and `-h` on other options.\n- Suppressing stderr errors - quiet narrows the report, not failure reporting.\n- Changes to scoring, thresholds, phase recommendation or the JSON schema - the feature changes rendering only.\n- Updating prose docs that mention the script but never read its output (README, workflow references) - their invocation examples stay valid.\n\n### Files to Change\n\n| File Path | Change Type | Description |\n|-----------|-------------|-------------|\n| `.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/recommend-level.sh` | Modify | Add the `QUIET_OUTPUT` global, the `--quiet` parser case, the quiet dispatch branch and the two help entries. |\n<!-- /ANCHOR:scope -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:requirements -->\n## 4. REQUIREMENTS\n\n### P0 - Blockers (MUST complete)\n\n| ID | Requirement |\n|----|-------------|\n| REQ-001 | The argument parser accepts `--quiet`, alone or alongside existing flags, and sets `QUIET_OUTPUT=true`; unknown-option handling is unchanged. |\n| REQ-002 | With `--quiet` and no `--json`, stdout is exactly one line matching `^Recommended Level: [0-3] \\((Quick\\|Baseline\\|Verification\\|Full)\\)$`, terminated by one newline, and the exit code is 0. |\n| REQ-003 | Without `--quiet`, stdout is byte-identical to the pre-change output for the same arguments, including the leading blank line and the phase section. |\n\n### P1 - Required (complete OR user-approved deferral)\n\n| ID | Requirement |\n|----|-------------|\n| REQ-004 | `--quiet --json`, in either order, prints the existing JSON payload unchanged; quiet neither truncates nor mixes with JSON. |\n| REQ-005 | `--help` lists `--quiet` with a one-line description, and the header OPTIONS comment matches the help text. |\n\n> Acceptance criteria for these requirements live in `acceptance-criteria.md`,\n> which is the document that decides whether this packet may close.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:requirements -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:success-criteria -->\n## 5. SUCCESS CRITERIA\n\n- **SC-001**: `bash .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/recommend-level.sh --loc 500 --files 15 --quiet | wc -l` prints `1`.\n- **SC-002**: `diff` between a baseline capture and the post-change default invocation prints nothing for the same arguments.\n- **SC-003**: `bash -n recommend-level.sh` exits 0 and `--help` output contains a `--quiet` row.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:success-criteria -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:risks -->\n## 6. RISKS & DEPENDENCIES\n\n| Type | Item | Impact | Mitigation |\n|------|------|--------|------------|\n| Dependency | `bash` 3.2+ and coreutils (`grep`, `wc`, `diff`) | None; the script already requires both | No new runtime; keep the implementation to builtins and `echo`. |\n| Risk | The quiet line drifts from the label the default report prints | Medium - a caller parses the wrong text | Render both from `RECOMMENDED_LEVEL` and `LEVEL_NAME`; AC-002 pins the exact line. |\n<!-- /ANCHOR:risks -->\n\n---\n\n\n## 7. NON-FUNCTIONAL REQUIREMENTS\n\n### Performance\n- **NFR-P01**: The quiet path runs the same scoring and spawns no subprocess; wall time stays within 5% of the default form for the same arguments.\n\n### Security\n- **NFR-S01**: No new input, file or credential is read; the flag only selects an output branch, so there is no auth surface to test.\n\n### Reliability\n- **NFR-R01**: Exit codes are unchanged - 0 on success, 1 on the existing validation errors - and `--quiet` never suppresses a stderr error.\n\n---\n\n## 8. EDGE CASES\n\n### Data Boundaries\n- Empty input: no `--loc` or `--files` still exits 1 with the existing stderr error; quiet does not change validation.\n- Maximum length: `--loc 100000 --files 1000 --quiet` still prints one line, because scoring caps are untouched.\n\n### Error Scenarios\n- External service failure: N/A - the script makes no network call.\n- Network timeout: N/A - the script makes no network call.\n- Invalid numeric value: the existing stderr error and exit 1 survive `--quiet`.\n\n### State Transitions\n- Partial completion: N/A - the script is a single pass with no saved state.\n- Session expiry: N/A - the script holds no session.\n- Repeated `--quiet`: idempotent, `QUIET_OUTPUT` stays true.\n- `--quiet --json` in either order: JSON output wins, so the combination is harmless.\n- `--quiet --help`: help prints in full and exits 0, because help is not the report.\n\n---\n\n## 9. COMPLEXITY ASSESSMENT\n\n| Dimension | Score | Triggers |\n|-----------|-------|----------|\n| Scope | 4/25 | Files: 1, LOC: ~10, Systems: 1 |\n| Risk | 2/25 | Auth: N, API: N, Breaking: N |\n| Research | 2/20 | Read one script's parser and output dispatch |\n| Multi-Agent | 0/15 | Workstreams: 1 |\n| Coordination | 1/15 | Dependencies: 0 |\n| **Total** | **9/100** | **Level 3** |\n\nThe score covers the change itself, which the script's own thresholds would place at Level 0. This packet carries Level 3 because the authoring track scaffolds every packet at that level; the extra documentation is track overhead, not a signal that the change is architecturally risky.\n\n---\n\n## 10. RISK MATRIX\n\n| Risk ID | Description | Impact | Likelihood | Mitigation |\n|---------|-------------|--------|------------|------------|\n| R-001 | The quiet line drifts from the label in the default report | M | L | Both render from the same two variables; AC-002 pins the exact line. |\n| R-002 | `--quiet --json` mixes two output formats | M | L | The JSON branch is evaluated first; AC-004 covers both flag orders. |\n| R-003 | A caller assumes `--quiet` also hides errors | L | M | State \"report only, stderr unchanged\" in help and in AC-005. |\n\n---\n\n## 11. USER STORIES\n\n### US-001: One parseable line for callers (Priority: P0)\n\n**As a** CI step or wrapper script, **I want** `recommend-level.sh` to print only the recommended-level line when asked, **so that** I can choose a documentation depth without parsing a report.\n\n**Acceptance criteria:** see `acceptance-criteria.md` (rows referencing this story).\n\n---\n\n### US-002: Default report stays intact (Priority: P1)\n\n**As a** maintainer of the script, **I want** the default report and the JSON payload untouched, **so that** existing human workflows and documented examples keep working.\n\n**Acceptance criteria:** see `acceptance-criteria.md` (rows referencing this story).\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:questions -->\n## 12. OPEN QUESTIONS\n\n- None. The flag scopes to the text report, `--json` takes precedence, and no short alias is added.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:questions -->\n\n---\n\n## RELATED DOCUMENTS\n\n- **Implementation Plan**: See `plan.md`\n- **Task Breakdown**: See `tasks.md`\n- **Verification Checklist**: See `tasks.md`\n- **Decision Records**: See `decision-record.md`\n\n---\n","_meta":{"cognition.ai/linesAdded":57,"cognition.ai/linesRemoved":57}}],"rawInput":{"file_path":"/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-michelkerkmeester-MEGA-Development-Code-Environment-Public/fcd93cd7-b3f2-45e6-b976-87fabe792df3/scratchpad/speed-loop/w1eb206b128/tree/specs/zz-bench-authoring/001-recommend-level-quiet-flag/spec.md"},"_meta":{"cognition.ai/inferenceToolName":"write"}}
